{"id":108155,"title":"Adaptive, multiresolution visualization of large data sets using parallel octrees.","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=multiresolution volume rendering","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/m2/1/high_res_d/11842.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"133999602b0cc1ec9224f5fe5d9867593e99eebd300a599c838210d993fb505f","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793234912.4680388,"text_chars":32059,"abstract":"The interactive visualization and exploration of large scientific data sets is a challenging and difficult task; their size often far exceeds the performance and memory capacity of even the most powerful graphics work-stations. To address this problem, we have created a technique that combines hierarchical data reduction methods with parallel computing to allow interactive exploration of large data sets while retaining full-resolution capability. The hierarchical representation is built in parallel by strategically inserting field data into an octree data structure. We provide functionality that allows the user to interactively adapt the resolution of the reduced data sets so that resolution is increased in regions of interest without sacrificing local graphics performance. We describe the creation of the reduced data sets using a parallel octree, the software architecture of the system, and the performance of this system on the data from a Rayleigh-Taylor instability simulation.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/m2/1/high_res_d/11842.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=multiresolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=adaptive resolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=hierarchical volume rendering wavelets multiresolution","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=adaptive octree volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=parallel cell projection volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=octree level of detail rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=bottom-up octree construction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=wavelet based multiresolution rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=adaptive volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=multi-resolution volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=dynamic adaptive octree grid","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=multi-resolution data management","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=octant method volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=mpi octree volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=domain based octree volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=coarse mesh traversal volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=wavelet pruning volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=dynamic octree construction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=mpi parallel slice volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc624851/?q=adaptive point insertion volume rendering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"16751-parallel-octree-data-reduction.md","name":"Parallel Octree Data Reduction","k":1}]}